  "version": "0.1.0",
  "lastUpdated": "2026-08-11",
  "notes": [
    "DEMO DATA. Not a nutrition data source. These twelve foods exist so the UI has something to render before the FoodData Central mirror is built, and nothing outside lib/demo may import this file.",
    "per-100g values are transcribed by hand from published USDA composition data and are approximate. They will be deleted, not corrected, once the FDC mirror lands.",
    "fdcId is null throughout, following the convention in nutrients.json: a hand-written FDC ID silently links to the wrong food, which is worse than no link at all.",
    "phytonutrients: null means NO DATA — the food is not in USDA's flavonoid, isoflavone, or proanthocyanidin databases. That is the honest state for most foods (~500 covered against FoodData Central's 600,000) and the UI must render it as 'no data', never as 0. See CLAUDE.md rule 5.",
    "A key of 0 inside a phytonutrients block is a MEASURED zero and is different from an absent key. Blueberries genuinely contain no flavones; sweet potato genuinely contains no lutein. Both are real zeros and render as 0.",
    "Nutrient keys absent from a nutrients block are also 'no data', not zero. Real FDC rows are full of gaps."
  ],

